  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to ballots for absentee voters",
    "basePrintNo": "S3135",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3135-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 34,
       "fullName": "Alessandra Biaggi",
       "imgName": "1051_Alessandra_Biaggi.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1231,
       "sessionMemberId": 1229,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "BIAGGI"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §7-122, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3135\n\nSPONSOR: MYRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to ballots for absentee\nvoters\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo ensure that absentee ballots match ballots for primary elections.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends subdivision 1(a) of § 7-122 of the election\nlaw to ensure that ballots for absentee voters. shall be, as nearly as\npracticable, in the same form as those to be voted in the district on\nelection day.\n\nSection 2 of the bill is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe existing law on absentee ballots for primary elections omits party\nposition of ward, town, city or county committee due to lack, of space\non ballots from the time that lever machines were used to cast votes.\nThis change would update the law and ensure that Election Day ballots\nand absentee ballots match.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
